{{Quote|My parents were criminals. They were arrested when I was three. I was raised in an Imperial Kinder-block.''"<br />"''Well&hellip; Nothing delicate about that, is there?|Dedra Meero and Eedy Karn|audio=DedrasParents-Harvest.flac|<ref name="Harvest" />}}
The [[human]] [[Dedra Meero]], a [[Homeworld|native]] of<ref name="2023 Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars|cardname=Dedra Meero|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/370777/cid/22170409/2023-Topps-Star-Wars-79-Dedra-Meero}}</ref> the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]],<ref name="CGttSWG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> was placed in a '''facility'''<ref name="Explained">{{SW|url=news/andor-explained-season-2-highlights-episodes-1-2-3|text=''Andor'' Explained: Episodes 1-3 - "One Year Later", "Sagrona Teema", and "Harvest"}}</ref> after her [[Dedra Meero's parents|parents]] were arrested when she was three [[Standard year|years]] old. She felt that she had everything she needed there growing up,<ref name="Harvest" /> but her [[time]] there resulted in her becoming a cold, calculating, emotionally bankrupt servant of the [[Galactic Empire]] and the facility itself later became an [[Imperial Kinder-block]].<ref name="Explained">{{SW|url=news/andor-explained-season-2-highlights-episodes-1-2-3|text=''Andor'' Explained: Episodes 1-3 - "One Year Later", "Sagrona Teema", and "Harvest"}}</ref> In [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Date">"[[One Year Later]]" dates the events of "[[Harvest]]" to [[4 BBY]].</ref> Meero informed [[Eedy Karn]], the [[Parent|mother]] of her partner [[Syril Karn]], about her childhood at the facility, causing Eedy to call her upbringing indelicate and claim that at the facility she had lacked a mother's love, although Meero responded that the children at the facility had not known what they were missing out on.<ref name="Harvest" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|He had said she had come from something really twisted. And then they managed to do it in one line: 'I grew up in an Imperial kinder-block.' There you go. Now you understand everything. She grew up with no touch, no love, no care, nothing. She grew up in a regime.|Denise Gough|<ref name="Couple">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-interview-denise-gough-kyle-soller|text=Even these ''Andor'' Stars Were Creeped Out by the Series' Strangest Power Couple}}</ref>}}
The Imperial Kinder-block was first mentioned in "[[Harvest]]," the third episode of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the [[Disney+]] live-action show ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'',<ref name="Harvest" /> which aired on [[April 22]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> During early development, the show's creator and executive producer, [[Tony Gilroy]], considered making an episode showing Dedra's unconventional childhood as a ward of the state in the facility. Instead, he chose to present this information with a single line, but this meant that the actress portraying Meero knew the character's twisted origin, viewing her as having grown up with no love, touch, or care.<ref name="Couple" />

